IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-2-explanations`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`
IMPORT `chapter-18-forgery`

§ `Chapter 18 -- Aggravated forgery, forged documents, false instruments and accounts`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 466, 467, 468, 469, 470, 471, 472, 473, 473A, 473B, 473C, 474,
-- 475, 476, 477, 477A.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Everything in this module stands on, or beside, s 463 forgery (already encoded in
-- `chapter-18-forgery.l4`). Four sections aggravate it by the kind of document forged
-- (ss 466, 467) or the purpose of the forger (ss 468, 469). s 470 names the product.
-- ss 471 and 474 punish the user and the possessor, who need not be the forger.
-- ss 472, 473, 475 and 476 reach the tools -- counterfeit seals, plates and
-- authenticating marks. ss 473A to 473C are the 2019 false-instrument offences and
-- their definition of "prejudice". s 477 is destruction rather than making. s 477A is
-- falsification of an employer's accounts and needs no false document at all.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED. s 465 is the punishment section for forgery and is not
-- encoded. The punishment differentials inside ss 471 and 474 are likewise not decided.

§§ `Sections 466 to 469 -- Aggravated forgery`

-- Each is "whoever forges" or "whoever commits forgery", plus one thing more. So each
-- conjoins `constitutes forgery` (s 463 on s 464) with either a description of the
-- document (ss 466, 467) or a purpose of the forger (ss 468, 469).
--
-- s 466 speaks of a "document or electronic record"; s 467 of a "document" only. The
-- two description facts follow that wording. s 469 is satisfied by intention OR by
-- knowledge that the document is likely to be so used, which is one disjunctive fact.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 466"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes forgery of a court record, public register or official document under Penal Code 1871 section 466
GIVEN d IS A `Document Making` @desc The s 463 and s 464 facts of the forgery itself.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The s 464 making must be dishonest or fraudulent.
      fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc The document forged purports to be a court record or proceeding, a register of birth, baptism, marriage or burial, a public servant's register or official certificate, an authority to sue, defend or confess judgment, or a power of attorney.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes forgery of a court record or public register` d f fd IF
        `constitutes forgery` d f
    AND fd's `the document or electronic record purports to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice or a register of birth baptism marriage or burial or a register kept by a public servant as such or a certificate document or electronic record purporting to be made by a public servant in his official capacity or an authority to institute or defend a suit or to take any proceedings in it or to confess judgment or a power of attorney`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 467"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes forgery of a valuable security, will or receipt under Penal Code 1871 section 467
GIVEN d IS A `Document Making` @desc The s 463 and s 464 facts of the forgery itself.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The s 464 making must be dishonest or fraudulent.
      fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc The document forged purports to be a valuable security, a will, an authority to adopt, an authority over a valuable security or over money or movable property, or an acquittance or receipt.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes forgery of a valuable security or will` d f fd IF
        `constitutes forgery` d f
    AND fd's `the document purports to be a valuable security or a will or an authority to adopt a child or purports to give authority to any person to make or transfer any valuable security or to receive the principal interest or dividends on it or to receive or deliver any money movable property or valuable security or purports to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money or the delivery of any movable property or valuable security`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 468"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes forgery for the purpose of cheating under Penal Code 1871 section 468
GIVEN d IS A `Document Making` @desc The s 463 and s 464 facts of the forgery itself.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The s 464 making must be dishonest or fraudulent.
      fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc The forger intends that the document forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes forgery for the purpose of cheating` d f fd IF
        `constitutes forgery` d f
    AND fd's `intends that the document or electronic record forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 469"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes forgery for the purpose of harming a person's reputation under Penal Code 1871 section 469
GIVEN d IS A `Document Making` @desc The s 463 and s 464 facts of the forgery itself.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The s 464 making must be dishonest or fraudulent.
      fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc The forger intends that the document forged shall harm the reputation of any person, or knows that it is likely to be used for that purpose.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes forgery to harm reputation` d f fd IF
        `constitutes forgery` d f
    AND fd's `intends that the document or electronic record forged shall harm the reputation of any person or knows that it is likely to be used for that purpose`

§§ `Section 470 -- A forged document`

-- A false document or electronic record made wholly or in part by forgery is a forged
-- document or forged electronic record. It is a designation, and ss 471 and 474 turn
-- on the accused knowing or having reason to believe that a document answers to it.
-- The forger may be someone else, whose facts this record does not carry, so whether
-- the document was in fact made by forgery is a caller-asserted fact and is not
-- computed from `constitutes forgery` -- the same treatment s 410 gives to stolen
-- property.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 470"
@export Decide whether a document or electronic record is a forged document or forged electronic record within Penal Code 1871 section 470
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc A false document or false electronic record, made wholly or in part by forgery.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document is a forged document` IF
    fd's `the document or electronic record is a false document or false electronic record made wholly or in part by forgery`

§§ `Sections 471 and 474 -- Using and possessing a forged document`

-- s 471: fraudulently or dishonestly uses as genuine a document he knows or has reason
-- to believe to be forged. The fault is s 24 or s 25 and is taken from the Fault
-- record. "Punished in the same manner as if he had forged" is punishment only.
--
-- s 474: possession of a document known to be forged, intending that it shall
-- fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine. The section applies only "if the
-- document or electronic record is one of the descriptions mentioned in section 466"
-- or "in section 467" -- so one of the two descriptions is an element, and the choice
-- between them is punishment only. The fraud or dishonesty here qualifies the intended
-- future use, not the act of possessing, so it lives inside the intention fact and is
-- not taken from the Fault record.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 471"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes using as genuine a forged document under Penal Code 1871 section 471
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc Uses as genuine a document or electronic record, knowing or having reason to believe it to be forged.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements. The use must be fraudulent (s 25) or dishonest (s 24).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes using a forged document as genuine` fd f IF
        (`the act is done dishonestly` f OR `the act is done fraudulently` f)
    AND fd's `uses as genuine a document or electronic record`
    AND fd's `knows or has reason to believe the document or electronic record to be a forged document or forged electronic record`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 474"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes possessing a forged document with intent to use it as genuine under Penal Code 1871 section 474
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc Possession of a document of a s 466 or s 467 description, knowing it to be forged and intending that it shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes possession of a forged document` IF
        fd's `has in his possession a document or electronic record knowing it to be forged`
    AND fd's `intends that the document or electronic record shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine`
    AND (   fd's `the document or electronic record purports to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice or a register of birth baptism marriage or burial or a register kept by a public servant as such or a certificate document or electronic record purporting to be made by a public servant in his official capacity or an authority to institute or defend a suit or to take any proceedings in it or to confess judgment or a power of attorney`
         OR fd's `the document purports to be a valuable security or a will or an authority to adopt a child or purports to give authority to any person to make or transfer any valuable security or to receive the principal interest or dividends on it or to receive or deliver any money movable property or valuable security or purports to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money or the delivery of any movable property or valuable security`)

§§ `Sections 472 and 473 -- Counterfeit seals, plates and instruments for making an impression`

-- Each has two conduct limbs -- making or counterfeiting the seal, or possessing it
-- knowing it to be counterfeit -- and one intent: that it be used to commit a forgery
-- punishable under s 467 (s 472) or under any other section of this Chapter (s 473).
-- Neither requires that any forgery be committed.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 472 and 473"
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `makes or possesses a counterfeit seal` IF
        fd's `makes or counterfeits any seal plate or other instrument for making an impression`
    OR  fd's `has in his possession any such seal plate or other instrument knowing it to be counterfeit`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 472"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes making or possessing a counterfeit seal for a forgery punishable under section 467 under Penal Code 1871 section 472
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc Making, counterfeiting or knowingly possessing a counterfeit seal, plate or impression-making instrument, intending it to be used to commit a forgery punishable under s 467.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes making or possessing a counterfeit seal for a section 467 forgery` IF
        `makes or possesses a counterfeit seal` fd
    AND fd's `intends that the seal plate or instrument shall be used for the purpose of committing a forgery which would be punishable under section 467`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 473"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes making or possessing a counterfeit seal for a forgery punishable otherwise under Penal Code 1871 section 473
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc Making, counterfeiting or knowingly possessing a counterfeit seal, plate or impression-making instrument, intending it to be used to commit a forgery punishable under a section of Chapter 18 other than s 467.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes making or possessing a counterfeit seal for another forgery` IF
        `makes or possesses a counterfeit seal` fd
    AND fd's `intends that the seal plate or instrument shall be used for the purpose of committing a forgery which would be punishable under a section of Chapter 18 other than section 467`

§§ `Sections 473A, 473B and 473C -- Equipment for making a false instrument`

-- "Instrument" is defined for this Chapter by s 31A and includes documents, stamps,
-- seals, dies and any card, chip or device on which information is recorded.
--
-- s 473A is complete on making, or having custody or control of, a machine, implement,
-- paper or material that the accused KNOWS is or has been specifically designed or
-- adapted for making a false instrument. No intent beyond that knowledge is needed.
--
-- s 473B drops the knowledge that the equipment is for FALSE instruments -- it need
-- only be designed or adapted for making "any instrument" -- and substitutes a
-- two-part intent: (i) that the accused or another will make a false instrument with
-- it in order to induce a person to accept it as genuine, and (ii) that by so
-- accepting it the person does or does not do some act to a person's prejudice.
-- s 473C(3) extends "induce a person to accept" to inducing a machine to respond, and
-- that extension is written into the (i) fact.
--
-- s 473C defines prejudice. An act or omission is to a person's prejudice IF AND ONLY
-- IF it will produce one of the six results in s 473C(1)(a) to (f); s 473C(4) adds
-- the case of an act induced by a machine's response, which is deemed to be to a
-- person's prejudice; and s 473C(2) directs that an act the person has an enforceable
-- duty to do, and an omission of an act he is not entitled to do, are disregarded.
-- s 473C(5) widens "loss" in (a) to include not getting what one might get, and is
-- written into the (a) fact. So: the six results and the machine case are disjoined,
-- and the s 473C(2) disregard is a negated conjunct over the whole.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 473A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes making or possessing equipment for making a false instrument under Penal Code 1871 section 473A
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc Making, or having custody or control of, a machine, implement, paper or material known to be specifically designed or adapted for making a false instrument.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes possessing equipment for making a false instrument` IF
        fd's `makes or has in his custody or under his control a machine or implement or paper or other material`
    AND fd's `to his knowledge the machine implement paper or material is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any false instrument`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 473C"
@export Decide whether the act or omission intended to be induced is to a person's prejudice within Penal Code 1871 section 473C
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc The act or omission the accused intends to induce, tested against the six results in s 473C(1), the machine case in s 473C(4), and the s 473C(2) disregard.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act or omission intended to be induced is to a person prejudice` IF
        (   fd's `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in a person permanently or temporarily losing property including by not getting what he might get`
         OR fd's `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in a person being deprived of an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration`
         OR fd's `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in a person being deprived of an opportunity to gain a financial advantage otherwise than by way of remuneration`
         OR fd's `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in somebody being given an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration from a person`
         OR fd's `the act or omission intended to be induced will result in somebody being given an opportunity to gain a financial advantage from a person otherwise than by way of remuneration`
         OR fd's `the act or omission intended to be induced will be the result of a person having accepted a false instrument as genuine in connection with his performance of any duty`
         OR fd's `the act or omission intended to be induced is one induced by a machine responding to the instrument as if it were genuine`)
    AND (NOT fd's `the act intended to be induced is one the person has an enforceable duty to do or the omission intended to be induced is of an act the person is not entitled to do`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 473B"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes making or possessing equipment for making a false instrument with intent to induce prejudice under Penal Code 1871 section 473B
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc Making, or having custody or control of, equipment designed or adapted for making any instrument, intending that a false instrument be made with it to induce a person (or a machine) to accept it as genuine and thereby act or omit to act to a person's prejudice.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes possessing equipment for making a false instrument to induce prejudice` IF
        fd's `makes or has in his custody or under his control a machine or implement or paper or other material`
    AND fd's `the machine implement paper or material is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any instrument`
    AND fd's `intends that he or another person makes a false instrument using the machine implement paper or material in order to induce another person to accept it as genuine or to induce a machine to respond to it as if it were a genuine instrument`
    AND fd's `intends that by reason of so accepting it the person induced does or does not do some act`
    AND `the act or omission intended to be induced is to a person prejudice` fd

§§ `Sections 475 and 476 -- Counterfeit authenticating devices and marks`

-- Two conduct limbs -- counterfeiting the device or mark on or in a material, or
-- possessing material on or in which it has been counterfeited -- and one intent: that
-- it give the appearance of authenticity to a document then forged or thereafter to be
-- forged on that material. s 475 is the case where the device authenticates a s 467
-- document; s 476 is every other document or electronic record, so it is the same test
-- with that fact negated.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 475 and 476"
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counterfeits or possesses a counterfeit authenticating mark with intent` IF
        (   fd's `counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating a document or electronic record`
         OR fd's `has in his possession any material upon or in the substance of which any such device or mark has been counterfeited`)
    AND fd's `intends that the device or mark shall be used for the purpose of giving the appearance of authenticity to any document or electronic record then forged or thereafter to be forged on that material`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 475"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes counterfeiting a device or mark for authenticating a section 467 document under Penal Code 1871 section 475
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc Counterfeiting, or possessing material bearing, a counterfeit device or mark used to authenticate a document described in s 467, intending it to lend authenticity to a forged document.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes counterfeiting a mark for a section 467 document` IF
        `counterfeits or possesses a counterfeit authenticating mark with intent` fd
    AND fd's `the device or mark is used for the purpose of authenticating a document described in section 467`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 476"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes counterfeiting a device or mark for authenticating a document other than a section 467 document under Penal Code 1871 section 476
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc Counterfeiting, or possessing material bearing, a counterfeit device or mark used to authenticate a document or electronic record other than one described in s 467, intending it to lend authenticity to a forged document.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes counterfeiting a mark for another document` IF
        `counterfeits or possesses a counterfeit authenticating mark with intent` fd
    AND (NOT fd's `the device or mark is used for the purpose of authenticating a document described in section 467`)

§§ `Section 477 -- Fraudulent cancellation, destruction or secreting of a will or valuable security`

-- Three alternative mental states: fraudulently (s 25), dishonestly (s 24), or with
-- intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person. The conduct reaches
-- cancelling, destroying, defacing, secreting, the ATTEMPT to do any of those, and
-- committing mischief in respect of the document -- so no separate s 511 analysis is
-- needed. The document must be, or purport to be, a will, an authority to adopt a
-- child, or a valuable security.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 477"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes fraudulent cancellation, destruction or secreting of a will or valuable security under Penal Code 1871 section 477
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc Cancelling, destroying, defacing or secreting (or attempting to) a document which is or purports to be a will, an authority to adopt or a valuable security, or committing mischief in respect of it; done fraudulently, dishonestly, or with intent to cause damage or injury.
      f IS A Fault @desc Fault elements, for the fraudulent (s 25) or dishonest (s 24) routes.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes fraudulent cancellation of a will or valuable security` fd f IF
        (   `the act is done dishonestly` f
         OR `the act is done fraudulently` f
         OR fd's `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person`)
    AND fd's `cancels destroys or defaces or attempts to cancel destroy or deface or secretes or attempts to secrete a document or commits mischief in respect of it`
    AND fd's `the document is or purports to be a will or an authority to adopt a child or any valuable security`

§§ `Section 477A -- Falsification of accounts`

-- The accused must be a clerk, officer or servant, or employed or acting in that
-- capacity. Two conduct limbs, each done "intentionally and with intent to defraud":
-- destroying, altering, concealing, mutilating or falsifying the employer's books,
-- records, papers, securities or accounts; or making (or abetting) a false entry in
-- them, or omitting or altering (or abetting the omission or alteration of) a material
-- particular.
--
-- "Intent to defraud" is not the s 25 term -- s 25 defines "fraudulently" as intent
-- to deceive coupled with an intended advantage or detriment -- so it is not routed
-- through the Fault record and stays inside each conduct fact as the section words it.
-- Explanation 1 (a general intent to defraud suffices in the charge) removes a burden
-- and adds no limb. Explanation 2 (what makes a "set") widens what may be asserted.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 477A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes falsification of accounts by a clerk, officer or servant under Penal Code 1871 section 477A
GIVEN fd IS A `Forged Document` @desc A clerk, officer or servant who intentionally and with intent to defraud destroys, alters, conceals, mutilates or falsifies the employer's books, records or accounts, or makes a false entry in them or omits or alters a material particular.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes falsification of accounts` IF
        fd's `is a clerk officer or servant or is employed or acting in the capacity of a clerk officer or servant`
    AND (   fd's `intentionally and with intent to defraud destroys alters conceals mutilates or falsifies any book electronic record paper writing valuable security or account or a set of them which belongs to or is in the possession of his employer or has been received by him for or on behalf of his employer`
         OR fd's `intentionally and with intent to defraud makes or abets the making of any false entry in or omits or alters or abets the omission or alteration of any material particular from or in any such book electronic record paper writing valuable security or account or set of them`)

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes aggravated forgery` IF
        (   `constitutes forgery of a court record or public register` (a's `document making`) (a's `fault`) (a's `forged document`)
         OR `constitutes forgery of a valuable security or will` (a's `document making`) (a's `fault`) (a's `forged document`)
         OR `constitutes forgery for the purpose of cheating` (a's `document making`) (a's `fault`) (a's `forged document`)
         OR `constitutes forgery to harm reputation` (a's `document making`) (a's `fault`) (a's `forged document`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a forged document offence` IF
        (   `constitutes using a forged document as genuine` (a's `forged document`) (a's `fault`)
         OR `constitutes possession of a forged document` (a's `forged document`)
         OR `constitutes making or possessing a counterfeit seal for a section 467 forgery` (a's `forged document`)
         OR `constitutes making or possessing a counterfeit seal for another forgery` (a's `forged document`)
         OR `constitutes counterfeiting a mark for a section 467 document` (a's `forged document`)
         OR `constitutes counterfeiting a mark for another document` (a's `forged document`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a false instrument equipment offence` IF
        (   `constitutes possessing equipment for making a false instrument` (a's `forged document`)
         OR `constitutes possessing equipment for making a false instrument to induce prejudice` (a's `forged document`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes fraudulent cancellation of a will or valuable security` IF
        `constitutes fraudulent cancellation of a will or valuable security` (a's `forged document`) (a's `fault`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes falsification of accounts` IF
        `constitutes falsification of accounts` (a's `forged document`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
